<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-686] Allow for Unsigned Statistics in Binary Type</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-686</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;BinaryStatistics currently only have a min/max, which are compared as signed &lt;tt&gt;byte[]&lt;/tt&gt;. However, for real UTF8-friendly lexicographic comparison, e.g. for string columns, we would want to calculate the BinaryStatistics based off of a comparator that treats the bytes as unsigned.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12999290">PARQUET-686</key>
            <summary>Allow for Unsigned Statistics in Binary Type</summary>
